OpenACAI Endnight Loader contains original compatibility glue code by Alex Cooper.
It is intentionally built on top of BepInEx's Unity IL2CPP loader work and
RedLoader/SonsSdk's Sons Of The Forest modding work. OpenACAI preserves and
credits both upstream projects:

- BepInEx, by the BepInEx team: https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx
- Dobby, BepInEx fork based on jmpews/Dobby: https://github.com/BepInEx/Dobby
- RedLoader/SonsSdk, by Toni Macaroni: https://github.com/ToniMacaroni/RedLoader
- Tomlet and SemanticVersioning, used as small managed compatibility and SDK
  support dependencies while OpenACAI absorbs RedLoader/SonsSdk behavior.

Those upstream components remain under their own licenses and copyright notices.

This package includes the client-only Modstoke Client Companion. Its inventory
audit protocol and reader were adapted from the owner's private OpenACAI Admin
source. The owner authorized public source and binary distribution of these
Modstoke components and licensed the adapted client companion code under MIT.
Its scoped license is in `src/Modstoke.ClientCompanion/LICENSE` with
Copyright (c) 2026 Alex Cooper. This MIT grant does not apply to the separate
host Admin mod, which is not included in this package.

Third-party license texts for identified dependencies and incorporated source
are collected in `LICENSES/THIRD_PARTY/`. The RedLoader source tree contains
an LGPL-2.1 root license and a conflicting AGPL-2.0 package metadata value;
both are preserved and the conflict remains unresolved. This local snapshot is
not a corresponding, reproducible source release for the frozen preview ZIP.
